{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"caution","title":"Caution","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\nPlease use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" route option that is present during route configuration.\nSee the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../guide/not-found-errors.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Not Found Errors guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" class extends the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route"},{"type":"text","value":" class and can be used to create a not found route instance. A not found route instance can be passed to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routerOptions.notFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" option to configure a default not-found/404 route for every branch of the route tree."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"constructor-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor accepts an object as its only argument."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type:"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"Omit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./RouteOptionsType.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RouteOptions"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The options that will be used to configure the not found route instance."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { NotFoundRoute, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { Route as rootRoute } from './routes/__root'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst notFoundRoute = new NotFoundRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  component: () => <div>Not found!!!</div>,\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  notFoundRoute,\n})\n\n// ... other code","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"constructor-options","text":"Constructor options","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!CAUTION]\n> This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\n> Please use the `notFoundComponent` route option that is present during route configuration.\n> See the [Not Found Errors guide](../../guide/not-found-errors.md) for more information.\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` class extends the `Route` class and can be used to create a not found route instance. A not found route instance can be passed to the `routerOptions.notFoundRoute` option to configure a default not-found/404 route for every branch of the route tree.\n\n## Constructor options\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` constructor accepts an object as its only argument.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nOmit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>\n```\n\n- [RouteOptions](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n- Required\n- The options that will be used to configure the not found route instance.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { NotFoundRoute, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { Route as rootRoute } from './routes/__root'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst notFoundRoute = new NotFoundRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  component: () => <div>Not found!!!</div>,\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  notFoundRoute,\n})\n\n// ... other code\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: NotFoundRouteClass\ntitle: NotFoundRoute class\n---\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> This class has been deprecated and will be removed in the next major version of TanStack Router.\n> Please use the `notFoundComponent` route option that is present during route configuration.\n> See the [Not Found Errors guide](../../guide/not-found-errors.md) for more information.\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` class extends the `Route` class and can be used to create a not found route instance. A not found route instance can be passed to the `routerOptions.notFoundRoute` option to configure a default not-found/404 route for every branch of the route tree.\n\n## Constructor options\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` constructor accepts an object as its only argument.\n\n- Type:\n\n```tsx\nOmit<\n  RouteOptions,\n  | 'path'\n  | 'id'\n  | 'getParentRoute'\n  | 'caseSensitive'\n  | 'parseParams'\n  | 'stringifyParams'\n>\n```\n\n- [RouteOptions](./RouteOptionsType.md)\n- Required\n- The options that will be used to configure the not found route instance.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { NotFoundRoute, createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { Route as rootRoute } from './routes/__root'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen'\n\nconst notFoundRoute = new NotFoundRoute({\n  getParentRoute: () => rootRoute,\n  component: () => <div>Not found!!!</div>,\n})\n\nconst router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n  notFoundRoute,\n})\n\n// ... other code\n```\n"}
